{"ghsa_id":"GHSA-5hhx-4wrr-3j9g","cve_id":null,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/security-advisories/GHSA-5hhx-4wrr-3j9g","html_url":"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/security/advisories/GHSA-5hhx-4wrr-3j9g","summary":"Yielding in a component start function can lead to a host panic","description":"### Summary\r\n\r\nWhen Wasmtime ran a component start function which called an async-lowered import followed by a call to the `thread.yield` intrinsic function, it triggered a panic on the host side.\r\n\r\n### Details\r\n\r\nIn the aforementioned scenario, the runtime code responsible for resuming a guest thread became confused about which state the thread was in, mistakenly overwriting and dropping the internal fiber belonging to that thread.  Because Wasmtime-managed fibers must be disposed of explicitly before they are dropped, and because this one wasn't, the `drop` function panicked.\r\n\r\n### Impact\r\n\r\nEmbedder code which instantiates arbitrary components may be affected.","severity":"medium","author":null,"publisher":{"login":"alexcrichton","id":64996,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0OTk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64996?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton","html_url":"https://github.com/alexcrichton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/received_events","type":"